## 1 — The exact text at issue

`DECISIONS.jsonl` D-13 (2026-08-23T04:46:23Z, power G9), ruling **part 2**, verbatim:

> (2) THE UNEARNED service_health GREEN: RECORDED, NOT FIXED, AND SUTRADHARA WAS RIGHT NOT TO
> QUEUE IT. Three service assets read service_health='healthy' with no health_probe. That is a
> status with no detector — H4/§N.8, the campaign's founding defect, sitting live in the
> registry. **It is R0 substrate and R0 IS NOT OPEN**, so I13 forbids repairing it now no matter
> how cleanly it would go. But 'not now' must not mean 'not written down': it is recorded HERE,
> durably and greppably, and **routed to R0 stage-1 intake (§8.6)** as pre-measured input so R0
> starts from fact. It is additionally to be carried into the Defect Register through the
> GENERATOR's input, never by hand-editing the workbook (§16: generated, never hand-edited).
> Whoever opens R0 must treat these three as a named finding, not rediscover them.

(Emphasis added. The two bolded clauses are the only part this note disputes.)

## 2 — The four assets, with their live `rung` queried from `asset_registry`

The `rung` column did not exist when D-13 was written; migration 590 added it at
